                "They are divided based on water availability into: Moist Deciduous Forests (100 to 200 cm rainfall) and Dry Deciduous Forests (70 to 100 cm rainfall).",
                "Moist Deciduous Forests are characterized by Teak (Tectona grandis), Sal (Shorea robusta), Sandalwood (Santalum album), Shisham, Mahua, and Mulberry.",
